{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"polygon-calculator UI copy.additionalFaqs.0.answer","detected_language":"es","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"polygon-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.0.answer","keys":["polygon-calculator.copy.additionalFaqs.0.answer"],"locale":"es","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"La calculadora deriva el apotema y el perímetro, y luego utiliza el área = perímetro × apotema ÷ ZXQPH0000QXZ.","record_id":"ad188a50e8cf66fab81a78fd83f170ffae537ab61e94269a1dfa785a5972a137","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"40843674935","seconds":2.042685798125035,"source":"Enter its number of sides and one known measurement. The calculator derives the apothem and perimeter, then uses area = perimeter × apothem ÷ 2.","source_commit":"e1f72394198c1a94fce448ea14cd79b496701273","source_hash":"77a2c905591ae76259757a86aa734f07a31d4c2565bdc6b57f6e87102cde152c","status":"machine-draft","translation":"La calculadora deriva el apotema y el perímetro, y luego utiliza el área = perímetro × apotema ÷ 2.","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
{"approved":false,"back_sample":null,"beam_size":2,"checks":{"no_residual_markers":true,"nonempty":true,"not_truncated":true,"protected_values":true,"translated":true},"context":"prime-number-checker UI copy.method.paragraphs.0","detected_language":"es","format":"usefulverse-background-draft-v1","key":"prime-number-checker.copy.method.paragraphs.0","keys":["prime-number-checker.copy.method.paragraphs.0"],"locale":"es","model":"google/madlad400-3b-mt","raw_translation":"Un número primo es un número entero mayor que uno con exactamente dos divisores positivos: uno y sí mismo. Los números compuestos tienen otro divisor. El cero y el uno no pertenecen a ninguna de las categorías. Esta página acepta dígitos enteros no negativos y rechaza decimales, signos por debajo de cero y la notación de exponentes.","record_id":"ad122ad8b6b10fcf5a7dcd6616da64d54b7c971459ae878302ddd3274513d800","revision":"fa184c675da0b5c9e1c8694fccd4e12e2d422094","run_id":"41028627586","seconds":1.6676982882499942,"source":"A prime is an integer greater than one with exactly two positive divisors: one and itself. Composite numbers have another divisor. Zero and one belong to neither category. This page accepts nonnegative integer digits and rejects decimals, signs below zero and exponent notation.","source_commit":"0795f2ac94fd96942ab121fbeaaccf7766f584d4","source_hash":"9b0f4c9201ca71380dbc3ab4897f4f8a2897f056cc79dd209918b984dc51be72","status":"machine-draft","translation":"Un número primo es un número entero mayor que uno con exactamente dos divisores positivos: uno y sí mismo. Los números compuestos tienen otro divisor. El cero y el uno no pertenecen a ninguna de las categorías. Esta página acepta dígitos enteros no negativos y rechaza decimales, signos por debajo de cero y la notación de exponentes.","truncated":false,"warnings":[]}
